" Tests for claude#session#project_dir() — the slugified cwd Claude's own
" CLI uses under ~/.claude/projects/. Every character that isn't a letter
" or digit becomes '-', not just '/': a cwd with a dot or underscore in it
" (a "pedro.cordeiro" home directory, a "github.com" path segment, an
" "e2e_extraction" worktree) must still slugify to the real directory the
" CLI itself writes transcripts under, or has_transcript()/is_foreign_active()
" silently see nothing and every resume wrongly falls through to
" --session-id, which the CLI then refuses as "already in use".

Execute (only the path separator is slugified in a plain path):
  AssertEqual expand('~/.claude/projects/') . '-Users-me-project',
        \ claude#session#project_dir('/Users/me/project')

Execute (a dot in the cwd is slugified too):
  AssertEqual expand('~/.claude/projects/') . '-Users-pedro-cordeiro-project',
        \ claude#session#project_dir('/Users/pedro.cordeiro/project')

Execute (an underscore in the cwd is slugified too):
  AssertEqual expand('~/.claude/projects/') . '-Users-me-repo-e2e-extraction',
        \ claude#session#project_dir('/Users/me/repo-e2e_extraction')

Execute (a leading dot segment produces a doubled dash, matching the real CLI):
  AssertEqual expand('~/.claude/projects/') . '-Users-me--vim-bundle-plugin',
        \ claude#session#project_dir('/Users/me/.vim/bundle/plugin')

Execute (a mixed path with dots, underscores and dashes matches the real CLI layout):
  AssertEqual
        \ expand('~/.claude/projects/')
        \ . '-Users-pedro-cordeiro-go-src-github-com-DataDog-datadog-agent-e2e-extraction',
        \ claude#session#project_dir(
        \   '/Users/pedro.cordeiro/go/src/github.com/DataDog/datadog-agent-e2e_extraction')
